{"user": "Does the corner matter that much?I think if they took the corner, they'd only flip over one of my pieces?", "user_ts": "2026-08-21T20:40:01.046041+00:00", "assistant": "Yes \u2014 even if **White\u2019s h1 corner only flips your g2 disc**, it still matters a lot:\n\n- That\u2019s an immediate **2-disc swing**: White gains **h1** and your **g2** changes back.\n- More importantly, **h1 can never be flipped**, so it\u2019s a permanent disc.\n- Your big flip from **g2** may be temporary; the corner is not.\n\nSo the key question isn\u2019t \u201chow many does White flip on h1?\u201d but: **after g2 \u2192 h1, do your 5 flipped discs actually stay yours by the end?**", "assistant_started_ts": "2026-08-21T20:40:06.637923+00:00", "assistant_ts": "2026-08-21T20:40:08.551911+00:00", "annotation_user": {"final": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "consensus": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "votes": {"Think Aloud": 3, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 3, "Common Ground Question": 1}, "confidence": {"Think Aloud": 1.0, "Knowledge Deficit Question": 1.0, "Common Ground Question": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "llama": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question"], "sonnet": ["Think Aloud", "Knowledge Deficit Question", "Common Ground Question"]}, "n_valid": 3, "min_votes": 2, "no_majority": false, "needs_review": false, "arbiter_used": false}, "annotation_assistant_fine": {"final": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "consensus": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "votes": {"Local Justification": 3, "General Principle": 3, "Positive Feedback": 2, "Prompt": 1, "Hint": 1}, "confidence": {"Local Justification": 1.0, "General Principle": 1.0, "Positive Feedback": 0.6666666666666666, "Prompt": 0.3333333333333333, "Hint": 0.3333333333333333}, "per_model": {"gpt": ["Local Justification", "General Principle", "Positive Feedback"], "s